// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27f/petal_security_viz.t27 -- petal Ti (SECURITY, plan row 26), the interactive visualization of
; the secret gate. Refs epic t27#12173 (issue t27#12318). Built on the shared contract
; specs/t27f/viz_contract.t27, in the pattern of the reference petal specs/t27f/petal_specs_viz.t27;
; it agrees with row 26 of
; specs/t27f/petal_viz_plan.t27 (reps 276 = list + trace + badge, truth VERIFIED).
; --
; What it answers: "Which secret-gate layer would stop this change, and on which rule?" The reader sees
; twelve fixture changes as a list (one line per change: the layer that stops it, or none, and the rule),
; steps through the three layers in the order a change meets them (the trace: which layers ran, which one
; stopped it, which rule fired, which allowlist excused it) and flips ONE fact for every change at once
; (hooks not installed, a commit or a push with --no-verify, a push that never had a local commit, a key
; name the rule does not list, a literal one character under the minimum, a value that is a reference, a
; placeholder word) to watch the stopping layer and the trace recompute.
; --
; Source of truth: specs/policy/secret_gate.t27 (module PolicySecretGate). It exposes ONE function, the
; writer of the gitleaks config that all three layers read: gitleaks_toml, and the pinned length
; TOML_LEN. This petal calls the writer and asks the written BYTES (with buf_has from specs/claw/text.t27,
; the same helper the source tests use) what the config says: whether the default rules are on, whether
; the custom rule exists, which key-name words it lists, the minimum literal length (read out of the
; regex, the number between braces), whether the value class excludes references, which placeholder
; words, which path and which line the allowlists excuse. Nothing of the config is copied here: a probe
; is a QUESTION to the bytes, so the answers move in the same commit as the rules.
; --
; Petal-side glue, said here and not hidden: secret_gate.t27 keeps no scan function and no layer data.
; The three layers are recorded in its HEADER PROSE only (pre-commit scans staged changes, pre-push scans
; commits not yet on a remote, CI scans the commits a pull request or push adds, all three reading the
; one config). So the layer table (which route reaches which layer), the route facts of each change
; (hooks installed, commit or push with --no-verify, local commit or not), the change shapes (plain,
; provider-shaped, password literal) and the premise that the default rules catch a provider-shaped
; change are a RECORDED petal-side fixture. The rules the config applies to those facts are the source's
; own bytes; the facts are not. This petal does not run gitleaks.
; --
; No secret is described by text: a change is a set of enums, flags and counts (a shape code, a key-name
; word id, a literal width as a number, a placeholder word id, a site code, a reference flag, four route
; flags). The only strings here are the short queries put to the config. Nothing in this file looks like
; a password, a key or a token, not even a fake one.
; --
; Layers of this spec:
;   L1 state       PtivState = one VizState (the contract) + the truth the last load reported; ptiv_apply
;                  forwards every event to the one reducer viz_apply and recomputes ONLY the truth.
;                  step = the layer reached (0..2), param = the flipped fact (0..8), item = the change.
;   L2 entities    change i = viz_ref(NODE, i); the focus order is the changes 0..11.
;   L3 fixture     twelve changes: four are stopped at the three layers, one by each route (normal,
;                  commit skipped, both hooks skipped, no local commit), and eight are not stopped, for
;                  four different reasons (placeholder, path, line, nothing matched).
;   L4 config      ptiv_cfg_*: questions put to the bytes gitleaks_toml writes.
;   L5 rules       ptiv_rule_for, ptiv_excuse_for, ptiv_layer_runs, ptiv_verdict, ptiv_state_of.
;   L6 flips       ptiv_flip: the contract's param flips ONE fact in EVERY change.
;   L7 views       list (stop layer and rule per change), trace (the layers up to the step), badge.
;   L8 truth       VERIFIED while every shown value is the config's rule over the recorded facts; DEMO
;                  while a flip is on (viz_may_claim false); CACHED and UNKNOWN are kept as loaded.
;   L9 host        ptiv_host: the badge, the list and the trace as three root slots; ptiv_reps is the
;                  set of reps it uses and equals the plan's row 26 (276).
; --
; Integer only: no floats. Pixel geometry is in frame coordinates (the origin is the frame's top-left
; corner), so a hit test and ptiv_host agree without an offset; embedded in another host the whole petal
; moves by the slot offset and nothing else.
; --
; Not claimed: no host draws this petal yet (wiring it into specs/t27os/glass_window.t27 is a child issue
; of the epic). The answers are the config text applied to a recorded fixture, not a scan of any real
; change: a host that fed real changes and ran the gate on them would report LIVE itself. The default
; rules of gitleaks are only on or off here (the config says useDefault); what they match is the
; recorded premise of the provider-shaped shape, not a reading of gitleaks.

